#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128928 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3eae4ea-fb38-5efa-843e-783327b82702" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Square Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "57abae04-4bc2-5fb4-a5b0-5c0c6c85f955" :question/math-academy-id "e-49" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2} \\sqrt{x-2}$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt{x-2}\n$$\n\n. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2) &= \\sqrt{2 - 2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{0} \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the graph of $y=f(x)$ \"starts\" at $x=2$. Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/a4/a4a64caff7a8b69454ffc8b93a1baad18bf3d93093b3c85a7c4fc3cb9762a2b4.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we notice that the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2^-} f(x) = \\textrm{DNE}\n$$\n\nwhile the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2^+} f(x) = 0\n$$\n\nSince the two limits are not equal, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2} f(x)= \\textrm{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128929 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad10ca6b-d130-559b-a201-15127659de13" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity of a Square Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1b850386-4730-512a-8408-932f7b6931b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-50" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow -\\infty} \\sqrt{3-x}$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt{3-x}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n![](images/d3/d3960d69c67ce1dbf731975ec1058f590ae6cfd61a3c3b04cb5632ce2eaf68aa.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -\\infty} f(x)= \\infty\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128932 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0631dd0e-a893-5099-8b52-e7a543e7f783" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "fbac92a0-de6c-556a-8bf1-030401a5df36" :question/math-academy-id "e-51" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -3} \\sqrt[3]{3x-2x^2}$." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=-3$ into the expression, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → - 3)\\sqrt[3]{3x - 2x^{2}} &= \\sqrt[3]{3(-3) - 2(-3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{-9 - 18} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\\n&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129023 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f945ef94-171c-5c19-adb3-f496408dc31b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit at Infinity of a Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "97cc7a63-900d-52e8-ad0b-2232309d6335" :question/math-academy-id "e-780" :question/problem "Compute $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} \\sqrt[3]{x-1}$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt[3]{x-1}\n$$\n\nLet's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n![](images/04/0481bb8a4e6058d3cc41069a210f7fc964d861c7071541432aa7422349410431.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} f(x)= \\infty\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3eae4ea-fb38-5efa-843e-783327b82702" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Square Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b285965a-e603-5a87-ad3a-7ce53eb039a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127820} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1ba97b-634b-5ab2-924d-cc9550d29b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127821} {:answer/id #uuid "d26cbbb3-365a-5044-b527-135d62972fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127822} {:answer/id #uuid "2f50ff08-d5af-50c7-b86a-03fd63f3058b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127823} {:answer/id #uuid "496462e6-999a-5292-869e-3d711ab01d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127824}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a75622fa-3456-516d-9426-1ef90c65e3c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127819}] :question/id #uuid "6d3a7b9f-edcc-5a37-bee6-71b22df3defa" :question/math-academy-id "q-3922" :question/problem "Calculate $lim_(x → 4^{-})\\sqrt{x - 4}$."}]}
